1. Ownership
   The software (source code, templates, stylesheets, scripts, translations
   and documentation) is protected by copyright. All rights remain with
   NEO Digital. This license does not sell any rights in the software; it
   grants a right of use.

2. Right of use
   NEO Digital grants a non-exclusive and non-transferable right to use the
   software on any number of websites.

   Without a licence key the use is free of charge. Condition: the credit
   line of the software in the chat window ("powered by" with the logo of
   NEO Digital linking to https://neo-digital.at) stays visible and
   unchanged. Without the credit
   line, the right of use for that website ends.

   With a valid licence key for the domain of a website, the credit line is
   not required on that website. Scope and term follow from the licence
   purchased.

   The relevant version is the version of the software that is available, at
   the time of the order (for free use: of the download), for the Contao
   long-term support version current at that time. That version works with
   that Contao version until its end of life according to Contao's release
   plan, under the requirements stated in the documentation; NEO Digital
   fixes errors of the software that prevent this during that time. This also
   applies when newer Contao long-term support versions have been released in
   the meantime. There is no entitlement to further updates, to new versions
   or to a version for a later Contao long-term support version, not even
   during a paid licence. NEO Digital may provide such versions at its own
   discretion. Support is not part of the licence and requires a separate
   agreement with NEO Digital.

3. You may
   a) install and configure the software under section 2;
   b) adapt configuration, templates, stylesheets and texts and modify the
      code for your own installations;
   c) as an agency, install it for your clients under section 2.

4. You may not
   a) distribute, publish, rent or sell the software or modified versions,
      except installing it under section 3 c;
   b) grant sublicenses;
   c) offer the software or substantial parts of it as your own product or as
      a service to third parties;
   d) remove or alter copyright and license notices;
   e) remove, hide, cover or alter the credit line under section 2 without a
      valid licence key, including by stylesheets, templates or changes to the
      code.

5. Third-party components
   Third-party components that are shipped or required (e.g. Contao, Symfony)
   are subject to their own licenses.

6. Warranty and liability
   a) Without a licence key the software is provided free of charge and as
      is; only the function under section 2 is committed.
   b) The answers of the assistant are generated by an AI model of a
      third-party provider. NEO Digital is not liable for their content, for
      content of external services and websites, or for costs incurred with
      chosen third-party providers.
   c) NEO Digital is not liable for actions that the assistant carries out in
      other systems through tools approved by the user (e.g. MCP servers), or
      for damage resulting from them. The same applies to skills and knowledge
      sources added by the user.
   d) Otherwise NEO Digital is not liable for slight negligence.
   e) The exclusions under b to d do not apply to damage caused by NEO Digital
      intentionally or through gross negligence, to injury to life, body or
      health, or to liability under product liability law.

7. Terms in the back end
   Before an assistant becomes visible to visitors and before the features of
   a licence edition are available, the user confirms the passages of that
   edition in the back end under "Access keys and licences". They are part of
   this license. The German version is binding; translations serve
   understanding. Changed passages are confirmed again.

8. Governing law and venue
   Austrian law applies, excluding its conflict-of-law rules and the
   UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. Venue is
   Graz, Austria, to the extent permitted by law.

